### RUN .setup for group A (dot1x-2026-10-23T1304): AWPTCM-T44270 EAP-PEAP,
### AWPTCM-T33360 Multiple Authentication, AWPTCM-T9032 EAP-TLS,
### AWPTCM-T33354 EAP-Notification.
### Declares ONLY swi_d (u2, the DUT), per STANDING-ORDERS §6.
###
### This session's dispatch gives `consoles: u2 ONLY` and triage established that NO case in
### this campaign needs u3 (swi_b) or u5 (swi_a). Both units are therefore absent from this
### file entirely -- no [switch], no [baudrates], no [power], no [powerlink], no
### [boot_from_flash] and no [portlink] touching them. With no entry at all, the framework's
### post-failure power cycle can never reach either unit.
###
### Every partner role these four cases need is played by the TESTBOX ITSELF:
###   The DUT is its own RADIUS server (`radius-server local`, nas 127.0.0.1) -- no external
###   RADIUS host is needed or used.
###   The SUPPLICANT is tb277: /sbin/wpa_supplicant 2.6 (-D wired) on eth4 for the real-crypto
###   cases (T44270 PEAP, T9032 EAP-TLS), and a scapy EAPOL helper (tools/eapol.py) for the
###   multi-supplicant and negative-control legs (T33360, T33354).
###   Capture is tcpdump on the box's eth4 leg, ALWAYS filtered `ether proto 0x888e`
###   (loop-protection emits 1 LDF/s across 57 instances and drowns an unfiltered capture).
### Not a partner switch anywhere.
###
### 🔴 SUPPLICANT LEG IS eth4 <-> port1.0.48, NOT eth3 <-> port1.0.10.
###    Enabling dot1x blocks a port until authentication succeeds; on port1.0.10 that would cut
###    the vlan10 L3 underlay and the box's own path to the DUT.
###
### 🔴 swi_d has TWO power supplies, outlets 1 AND 8 on 10.36.230.212. The framework's
###    [power] stanza takes ONE outlet, so a framework-initiated power cycle CANNOT actually
###    cut this unit: the cycle "completes", both PSU bays still read Ok, and only uptime
###    shows nothing happened. A real power cut needs both outlets together
###    (`tools/tb pdu tb277 10.36.230.212 1 cycle` AND `... 8 cycle`). Recorded here so a
###    silent no-op is never mistaken for a reboot.
### The box has NO deployed /home/st-art/configs/tb277.setup; never bind one.

[power]
pwr_d = (pdu, 10.36.230.212, 1)

[switch]
swi_d = /dev/u2

[baudrates]
swi_d = 115200

[stack]

[configured_stackport]

[powerlink]
swi_d = pwr_d

[boot_from_flash]
swi_d = True

[portlink]
tb-swi_d = eth3-port1.0.10, eth4-port1.0.48
